      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am updating my post for anyone in LINUX who is having the same issue:\n\nYou need to install windows versions of unity as well, through the Unity Hub. Open Unity Hub, open up the versions you have and click \"Add Modules\", and check off the Windows options and install them. \n\nThen when you go to upload your avatar upload through the Windows version in your editor. I have tested this with two people who were having this issue, and it works.",
